	["第7天"] = "Day 7",
	["第7次记录：同样的咒文，在葡萄藤旁低声念和在空地上直接念，结果完全不同。前者更柔和，后者更急躁。\n\n第11次记录：为受伤的卷毛狒狒处理伤口时，先安抚，再引导生命力流动，效果比直接催生血肉更好。\n\n第16次记录：蘑菇精喜欢亮晶晶的光点。若将绿焰拆成更细小的流萤状，它们会自己围过来，施术消耗反而降低。\n\n第22次记录：今天尤德拉之树的回响比昨天更清晰了一点。\n\n第31次记录：实验外溢的问题越来越明显，苹果长得太快，湖里的龟似乎也受了影响……不管了，等这一轮数据整理完再处理。\n\n（后面夹着几页零散的补记，字迹明显变快了。）"] = "7th Record: Same incantation, whispering it by the grapevines versus chanting it directly in the open field yields completely different results. The former is gentler, the latter more impatient. \n\n 11th Record: When treating the wounds of the curly-haired baboon, pacifying it first and then guiding the flow of life force is more effective than directly stimulating flesh and blood. \n\n 16th Record: Mushroom sprites like shiny light spots. If the green flame is broken down into finer firefly-like shapes, they will gather around on their own, reducing the consumption of casting. \n\n 22nd Record: Today, the echo of the Yodora Tree is a bit clearer than yesterday. \n\n 31st Record: The problem of experimental overflow is becoming more obvious; the apples are growing too fast, and the turtles in the lake seem to be affected... Never mind, I'll deal with it after this round of data is organized. \n\n (Behind it are a few loose supplementary notes, the handwriting is noticeably faster.)",
	["第8天"] = "Day 8",
