	["第四章 "] = "Chapter Four ",
	["第四纪元"] = "The Fourth Epoch",
	["第四纪元·众神纪元"] = "Fourth Epoch - Epoch of Gods.",
	["第四纪元最早的帝国是所罗门第一帝国，它统治了北大陆，染指了南大陆部分地区，首都在间海南岸，霍纳奇斯山脉源头，那是一座已经埋藏在历史和尘埃中的城市。"] = "The earliest empire of the Fourth Epoch was the First Solomon Empire. It ruled the Northern Continent and reached into parts of the Southern Continent. Its capital was on the south bank of the Sonia Sea, at the source of the Hornacis Mountains—a city already buried in history and dust.",
	["第四纪元等对话"] = "Fourth Epoch and other dialogues",
	["第四纪又称作众神纪元，是神明行走于大地的时代。在那个纪元中，有四大帝国存在，分别是所罗门帝国，图铎王朝，特伦索斯特帝国和拜朗帝国。"] = "The Fourth Epoch is also known as the Epoch of the Gods, an era when deities walked the earth. In that epoch, there were four great empires: the Solomon Empire, the Tudor Dynasty, the Trunsoest Empire, and the Balam Empire.",
	["第四纪的相关历史不确定的内容太多，你应该从现有的遗物入手研究，排除不确定因素。"] = "There are too many uncertain things about the history of the Fourth Epoch; you should start your research from existing relics and eliminate uncertain factors.",
	["第四节·简答题 \n\n一、请简述背誓之战爆发的时代背景和发展始末。\n \n二、请简述现代七大正神教会的教义宗旨、传教范围和影响力。\n\n三、请简述第四纪的国家及其政治实体的基本特点。\n\n四、请简述我国现行的货币制度以及币制改革的影响。\n\n五、请谈谈你对《谷物法案》颁布原因和实际作用的看法。\n\n……"] = "Section 4: Short Answer Questions \n \n 1. Please briefly describe the historical background and the development of the War of the Oath-Breaker. \n \n 2. Please briefly describe the doctrinal tenets, missionary scope, and influence of the seven major orthodox churches in the modern era. \n \n 3. Please briefly describe the basic characteristics of the countries and their political entities in the Fourth Epoch. \n \n 4. Please briefly describe our country's current monetary system and the impact of the currency reform. \n \n 5. Please share your views on the reasons for the promulgation of the \"Corn Laws\" and their actual effects. \n \n ...",
	["第四轮"] = "Rodada 4",
	["第四轮，请选择问题"] = "Fourth round, please choose a question",
	["第四阶段，声称也许应该在下雨前做点什么，但现在已经太迟了。"] = "Phase four, claim that perhaps we should have done something before it rained, but now it's too late.",
